#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This example demonstrates vehicle responses to a 40 km/h crosswind encountered 2 seconds into the simulation. The Closed Loop Driver Model is set to follow a straight path, so it calculates a steering wheel angle necessary to generate a countering yaw moment to the crosswind in order to maintain the designated path.
#
#Animation shapes representing the aerodynamic forces and moments on the vehicle have been linked on the Procedure screen to make it easier to visualize the vehicle's reactions to the crosswind.
#
#To see how this test was set up, including the wind speed and heading, click on the Procedure blue link "Crosswind Test w/ Steering" for more information.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

